Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:25:42 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(security): heredoc stripping by lexer ranges (bypass
 in 1e5b7d4, now on main)

The line-based stripHeredocBodies added in 1e5b7d4 treated `<<EOF` inside a quoted
string or a comment as a heredoc and dropped the following command lines from the
protected-path check: `echo "x<<EOF"` then `cat ../../notes.txt` was ALLOWED.
Heredoc bodies are now removed only at the exact source ranges recorded by the shell
lexer (quote, comment and here-string aware); any parse doubt keeps the raw text.
Probe H1-H7: 3 bypasses -> 0; the legitimate ../src import in a data heredoc stays allowed.
